{
  "id": "INV-CHALLENGE-ROUTING",
  "type": "runtime-invariant",
  "component": "Gate",
  "statement": "An implementer challenge against a gating test MUST be adjudicated by the critic (an independent read-only oracle), never by the coordinator's own judgement. Falsified if any challenge is resolved without routing to the critic, or if the coordinator rules on a challenge directly.",
  "verdict": "NOT-YET-BUILT",
  "severity": "medium",
  "overturned": false,
  "confidence": "high",
  "source": "consequential",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "lib/tau/factory/escalation.ex",
      "lines": "41",
      "what": "classify({:challenge, _}) -> {:\"E-CHALLENGE\", :unit} is the ONLY executable reference; a pure trigger->class mapping that presupposes a challenge already exists, not a route-to-critic adjudication"
    },
    {
      "file": "lib/tau/factory/escalation.ex",
      "lines": "39-46",
      "what": "Whole classify/1 body: no clause emits, captures, or rules on a challenge; it only classifies pre-formed triggers"
    },
    {
      "file": "lib/tau/factory/unit.ex",
      "lines": "224-358",
      "what": ":oracle FSM state handlers are the test-author phase (work_ready/worker_done/stalled/exit); no challenge capture or critic-routing clause exists in the Unit gen_statem"
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "Could not refute. Independent grep of lib/ for challenge|uphold|upheld|adjudicat|reject|oracle confirms the auditor: the only executable construct referencing a challenge is the pure Escalation.classify({:challenge, _}) -> {:\"E-CHALLENGE\", :unit} clause (escalation.ex:41). That clause merely maps an ALREADY-FORMED challenge trigger to an escalation class; it does not capture an implementer challenge, route it to the critic, or rule on it. There is no emitter of any {:challenge, ...} term anywhere in lib/ (only the classifier and its property test). The Unit gen_statem (unit.ex) has zero challenge handling; its :oracle state is the test-author phase, not challenge adjudication. The Gate.Oracle seam (gate.ex:150-194) dispatches the critic/reviewer gating halves, not challenges. No upheld/rej"
}
